WEBVTT

00:16.435 --> 00:19.335
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.335 --> 00:24.015
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:24.015 --> 00:25.915
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:25.915 --> 00:31.755
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.755 --> 00:39.295
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.295 --> 00:41.865
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:41.865 --> 00:45.895
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:45.895 --> 00:50.375
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.375 --> 00:53.545
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.545 --> 00:57.945
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:57.945 --> 01:01.785
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.785 --> 01:05.455
Mune no oku de

01:05.455 --> 01:08.755
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.755 --> 01:12.895
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:12.895 --> 01:15.895
toozakatte yukedomo

01:15.895 --> 01:22.965
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:42.025 --> 01:43.515
Wait!

01:48.865 --> 01:49.995
Nooooo!

01:49.995 --> 01:51.335
Morte!

01:51.335 --> 01:53.135
Instead of wasting all
our energy getting excited...

01:53.135 --> 01:55.165
why don't we just cool our heads a bit first?

01:55.165 --> 01:56.835
Whaddaya mean, "cool our heads"?!

01:56.835 --> 01:59.475
If we keep hanging around
here we'll freeze to death!

01:59.475 --> 02:02.545
I have a good idea, bear-o.

02:02.545 --> 02:04.945
Yeah, come to think of it, where is Toppy?

02:04.945 --> 02:07.485
I'm sure he's buried somewhere around here.

02:07.485 --> 02:10.485
- Toppy, where are you?!
- Kyrie, put on the fake ears!

02:10.485 --> 02:12.115
The fake ears?!

02:12.115 --> 02:15.525
Then you go to a human village
and start causing trouble, bear-o.

02:15.525 --> 02:19.125
At that point, Morte comes onto
the scene, also wearing fake ears...

02:19.125 --> 02:22.725
and she "defeats" you in
front of the whole village.

02:22.725 --> 02:26.035
She'll gain their trust, and even
wind up making friends with them...

02:26.035 --> 02:28.035
- but then the blue demon
comes and leaves them letter...
- Is he talking in his sleep again?

02:28.035 --> 02:29.975
- and then you...
- It's time for you to...

02:29.975 --> 02:33.135
Wake up!

02:41.715 --> 02:42.735
Bear-o?

02:43.185 --> 02:48.145
"There are Two Kinds of Pasts"

02:48.555 --> 02:51.395
Do you really think this
leads to the top of the cliff?

02:51.395 --> 02:55.095
Even if it doesn't, at least we
get to stay out of the cold, bear-o.

02:55.095 --> 02:57.435
This way I won't feel sleepy anymore, bear-o.

02:57.435 --> 03:01.425
This cave doesn't look like
it was formed naturally, does it?

03:03.205 --> 03:05.735
It looks like some kind of abandoned site...

03:05.735 --> 03:09.435
Wh-Wh-Wh-Whoops... Ow...

03:11.215 --> 03:14.615
A mu-mu-mu-mu-mu-mu-mu-mummy!

03:14.615 --> 03:16.755
What are all these mummies doing here?

03:16.755 --> 03:18.945
And so many...

03:20.125 --> 03:22.225
I don't see any injuries, bear-o.

03:22.225 --> 03:25.355
It doesn't look like they were
killed in any kind of attack, bear-o.

03:25.355 --> 03:29.125
In other words, maybe they all
came in here seeking shelter?!

03:29.125 --> 03:32.765
And if we keep standing around here,
this is exactly how we'll end up!

03:32.765 --> 03:34.395
Let's get going.

03:42.405 --> 03:45.605
What's going on? What's this?

03:46.575 --> 03:47.545
Morte?

03:47.545 --> 03:49.135
What's wrong, bear-o?

03:58.395 --> 04:00.565
I know this place...

04:00.565 --> 04:03.395
And now we bid our final farewell.

04:03.395 --> 04:05.155
Reve!

04:10.905 --> 04:12.265
No...

04:13.905 --> 04:15.395
No!

04:16.175 --> 04:17.975
- Hey!
- What is it, bear-o?!

04:17.975 --> 04:19.305
Morte!

04:26.655 --> 04:28.415
I know this place...

04:30.025 --> 04:32.955
Kyrie! What happened, bear-o?!

04:36.325 --> 04:38.365
I know this place...

04:38.365 --> 04:40.355
It's the village where I grew up, bear-o!

04:53.045 --> 04:58.615
That's right... it's the café
I was working at when I first met Morte.

04:58.615 --> 05:02.615
I remember seeing this
Help Wanted sign on the wall.

05:14.305 --> 05:16.235
Um, excuse me...

05:16.235 --> 05:19.035
Whatcha want? We ain't open yet.

05:19.035 --> 05:21.405
Oh! You wanna apply for the job?

05:21.405 --> 05:24.515
Listen, you... you got any
experience workin' in a kitchen?

05:24.515 --> 05:28.415
Absolutely! My specialty
is fried marinated sand whale!

05:28.415 --> 05:33.315
- It's exactly what happened
the day I first came to this town.
- As well as cooking, I can clean
and wash dishes and do most anything!

05:33.315 --> 05:35.485
I wonder what the heck's going on...

05:38.425 --> 05:42.395
You left the fortress. Where'd you go?

05:42.395 --> 05:45.565
Have you located those
Destruction Committee idiots?

05:45.565 --> 05:49.535
No. My clockwork soldiers
were in hot pursuit, but...

05:49.535 --> 05:54.275
it seems they lost them somewhere
in Dragon Valley on the winter continent.

05:54.275 --> 05:56.075
And the Destruct Code?

05:56.075 --> 05:59.115
Still missing, along with the fugitives.

05:59.115 --> 06:02.685
However, that may be just what you want.

06:02.685 --> 06:05.755
I seriously doubt they'll be able to
make it out of Dragon Valley alive anyway.

06:05.755 --> 06:09.025
The Destruct Code will meet the
same fate as the Destruction Committee...

06:09.025 --> 06:13.795
sealed away under the ice
of the winter continent for all time.

06:13.795 --> 06:15.565
That'll be meaningless!

06:15.565 --> 06:20.905
What do you mean? It'll mean
you've achieved your goal of saving the world.

06:20.905 --> 06:24.735
The Destruct Code means
nothing unless it's in my hands!

06:24.735 --> 06:27.445
It's not using the
Destruct Code that gives it meaning.

06:27.445 --> 06:31.575
It's having in my hands the
very power to destroy the world!

06:31.575 --> 06:34.545
That's the whole point.

06:34.545 --> 06:38.715
You're a real piece of work. In that case,
just go to Dragon Valley and get it.

06:38.715 --> 06:41.485
But I warn you... that valley
contains the Labyrinth of Memories.

06:41.485 --> 06:44.385
So don't let your guard down for a minute.

06:45.055 --> 06:48.325
This is...

06:48.325 --> 06:52.265
It's my... home.

06:52.265 --> 06:53.435
Eagle Master, sir...

06:53.435 --> 06:58.405
The so-called "Labyrinth of Memories"...
what kind of place is it?

06:58.405 --> 07:00.665
The Labyrinth of Memories...

07:01.745 --> 07:06.815
Once you get lost inside, that's it.
There's no coming back alive from that place.

07:06.815 --> 07:09.015
You're sucked into a dreamworld
filled with memories of your past...

07:09.015 --> 07:14.455
and you wander through the endless
nightmare. Until you wither away and die.

07:14.455 --> 07:19.295
His coffin is lying in state inside
the temple. Please go and see him later.

07:19.295 --> 07:22.265
Oh, that reminds me... did this belong to Reve?

07:22.265 --> 07:25.425
I found it among his things.

07:30.035 --> 07:35.645
So it's not? But he did keep it
on his person right to the very end.

07:35.645 --> 07:38.445
I think it must've been something
that was very important to him.

07:38.445 --> 07:41.845
So please take it, and
cherish it as a memento of him.

07:43.655 --> 07:47.125
This is the day Reve's coffin
was brought back home to the village...

07:47.125 --> 07:50.645
the day that I first laid
hands on the Destruct Code.

07:52.995 --> 07:55.555
Are you Reve's sister?

07:57.865 --> 08:02.205
I'm a member of the
Golden Lions. My name is Karna.

08:02.205 --> 08:04.905
I just want to ask you one thing...

08:04.905 --> 08:09.005
Have you ever heard the
stories of the Destruct Code?

08:09.005 --> 08:11.475
The "Destruct Code"?

08:11.475 --> 08:15.385
It's a legendary treasure said to
possess the power to destroy the world.

08:15.385 --> 08:17.355
The day just before Reve died...

08:17.355 --> 08:23.725
he apparently told some guys in his
squad that he'd found the Destruct Code.

08:25.195 --> 08:29.925
So if you find anything among Reve's
things that seems to fit that description...

08:29.925 --> 08:33.095
I'd appreciate it if you'd let me know.

08:39.375 --> 08:40.875
Stop for a second, Sis.

08:40.875 --> 08:43.715
What's this... you're already pooped?

08:43.715 --> 08:46.215
You're supposed to be the boy here.
That's the best you can do?!

08:46.215 --> 08:49.945
Listen, Sis... I have something
I want to talk to you about.

08:49.945 --> 08:51.455
What is it?

08:51.455 --> 08:57.025
You're my big sister,
so you might be against this...

08:57.025 --> 09:02.755
but I've been thinking
about joining the Golden Lions.

09:03.865 --> 09:06.095
Reve! What're you talking about?!

09:06.095 --> 09:08.205
You know how dangerous that is, don't you?

09:08.205 --> 09:12.475
But unless someone stands up and
does something, nothing's ever gonna change!

09:12.475 --> 09:15.745
Reve... but why you?!

09:15.745 --> 09:21.615
Sis, I wanna change the world!
I wanna free us from beastman control!

09:21.615 --> 09:23.915
No! Don't do it, Reve!

09:23.915 --> 09:28.225
You don't have to do anything like that!
You don't have to go changing the world!

09:28.225 --> 09:31.455
Just stay here and be with me! Please, Reve!

09:31.455 --> 09:35.425
Why're you just standing there?!
Do everything you have to to stop him!

09:35.425 --> 09:39.235
If you stop him now, he won't have to die!

09:39.235 --> 09:44.275
If you can just stop him now... Please!

09:44.275 --> 09:49.405
Stop him...

10:10.435 --> 10:12.835
D-Dad!

10:23.375 --> 10:25.815
There are two kinds of pasts.

10:25.815 --> 10:27.515
Pasts you want to forget...

10:27.515 --> 10:29.215
and pasts you'll never forget.

10:29.215 --> 10:33.185
What're you doing here, bear?

10:33.185 --> 10:34.525
Yappy!

10:34.525 --> 10:36.455
Everyone's waiting for us, bear.

10:36.455 --> 10:38.115
Let's hurry up and go, bear!

11:04.885 --> 11:08.985
So... you been hoppin' 'round
from one town to another, eh?

11:08.985 --> 11:12.055
I reckon that's the best way
for a young man like yourself.

11:12.055 --> 11:15.725
Go lotsa places, see lotsa things,
and grow up to be a man.

11:15.725 --> 11:18.195
It was the same with me when I was your age.

11:18.195 --> 11:21.035
So tell me... where'd you go before comin' here?

11:21.035 --> 11:23.065
Uh... um, well...

11:23.065 --> 11:26.505
Ah well, If you don't wanna tell me,
I ain't gonna force it outta you.

11:26.505 --> 11:32.175
I got a few skeletons in my own closet
that I don't wanna tell no strangers about.

11:34.045 --> 11:35.535
This place...

11:38.555 --> 11:40.675
Where am I?!

11:53.595 --> 11:54.805
Dad!

11:54.805 --> 11:57.805
Stop it! Stop showing me all these things!

11:57.805 --> 11:59.435
Daddy!

11:59.435 --> 12:01.425
Don't go!

12:04.245 --> 12:05.815
Daddy! Daddy!

12:05.815 --> 12:08.935
No... no more!

12:23.895 --> 12:27.435
No... no...

12:27.435 --> 12:29.665
No!

12:33.135 --> 12:36.435
Sis! Dinner's ready!

12:37.675 --> 12:42.315
Today we even have
your favorite... sand jellyfish!

12:42.315 --> 12:43.955
Hurry! Hurry!

12:43.955 --> 12:45.755
W-Wait a minute!

12:45.755 --> 12:48.125
You're late, Morte!

12:48.125 --> 12:50.795
Your ol' dad's getting pretty hungry here!

12:50.795 --> 12:54.925
Today we got some Sand Sea
fish for the first time in a long time.

12:54.925 --> 12:57.595
Dad! Mom!

12:57.595 --> 13:00.365
Go on... eat up!

13:00.365 --> 13:04.675
It looks good, doesn't it Sis? Let's eat!

13:04.675 --> 13:07.505
Let's eat...

13:07.505 --> 13:10.705
Open wide, Sis!

13:12.875 --> 13:14.515
It's so good!

13:14.515 --> 13:19.175
'Course it is! If your mother
made it, then it's gotta be good!

13:25.355 --> 13:30.025
With this gunpowder, we can finally
stand up to the beastmen on equal terms!

13:30.025 --> 13:32.895
Hey! Hurry it up there!

13:33.865 --> 13:35.905
I know... I'm hurrying!

13:35.905 --> 13:37.505
Need some help?

13:37.505 --> 13:39.735
Nah, I got it.

13:39.735 --> 13:41.745
This is my job.

13:41.745 --> 13:44.315
And besides, I'm getting
a pile of money for doing it.

13:44.315 --> 13:45.475
Are you a smuggler?

13:45.475 --> 13:48.645
Yeah... you got the cash,
I'll carry anything you want.

13:48.645 --> 13:50.185
Really?

13:50.185 --> 13:53.055
In that case, there is something
I'd like you to deliver for me.

13:53.055 --> 13:56.685
What is it? Weapons? Food?

13:56.685 --> 13:58.425
My words.

13:58.425 --> 13:59.425
Words?

13:59.425 --> 14:02.495
That's right. I've got a big sister
waiting all alone for me at home...

14:02.495 --> 14:05.095
and there's something
I want you to tell her for me.

14:05.095 --> 14:08.265
Tell her I'm sorry for making her worried...

14:08.265 --> 14:11.375
but that I will come home safe...

14:11.375 --> 14:13.835
and I will change the world.

14:13.835 --> 14:17.935
So to please just wait for me until then.

14:21.045 --> 14:24.055
So it was Morte's little brother after all.

14:24.055 --> 14:25.585
Reve, come here for a sec!

14:25.585 --> 14:26.515
Coming!

14:26.515 --> 14:27.885
All right, see you later!

14:27.885 --> 14:29.355
Sure.

14:31.895 --> 14:34.965
At that point, I turned around
and said this to him, bear-o...

14:34.965 --> 14:38.065
"Take a look at what's
on top of your head, bear-o!"

14:38.065 --> 14:44.275
That's right... and the look on that
White Bear's face was priceless, bear!

14:44.275 --> 14:45.805
- That's awesome!
- Those guys are so loud!

14:45.805 --> 14:47.035
I know!

14:49.205 --> 14:53.545
Yo girls, keep staring at me like that
and I'm gonna start blushing, bear-o!

14:55.045 --> 14:59.915
What say you and me lap up some
honey of love tonight, baby bear-o?

14:59.915 --> 15:01.885
Lap it up yourself, bub!

15:01.885 --> 15:03.375
Bear-o!

15:04.925 --> 15:07.595
Ow, bear-o.

15:07.595 --> 15:09.765
Where am I, bear-o?

15:09.765 --> 15:12.735
Where'd the Little Bear girls go, bear-o?

15:14.135 --> 15:16.635
Was that just a dream, bear-o?

15:16.635 --> 15:18.125
Oh no!

15:20.575 --> 15:23.975
What's happening?!
The energy's response is too weak.

15:23.975 --> 15:28.015
Is this really the Destruct Code?

15:28.015 --> 15:29.985
In that case...

15:33.755 --> 15:35.425
It's a beastman attack!

15:35.425 --> 15:36.655
Grab your weapons!

15:36.655 --> 15:39.085
- Hurry!
- Get going!

15:40.495 --> 15:41.825
- This way!
- Bring it here!

15:41.825 --> 15:44.135
Don't let the main force break through!

15:44.135 --> 15:45.595
The Alligator Master!

15:55.675 --> 15:58.475
Put the fire out! Hurry!

15:59.045 --> 16:00.885
The fire's gonna reach the gunpowder barrels!

16:00.885 --> 16:02.845
Give it up! You're not gonna make it!

16:02.845 --> 16:04.785
Get out of there!

16:22.905 --> 16:25.335
What is this?!

16:28.545 --> 16:30.135
So this is!

16:39.415 --> 16:40.715
Reve!

16:58.335 --> 17:00.675
So this little pipsqueak...

17:00.675 --> 17:03.445
Is the Destruct Code?!

17:03.445 --> 17:06.875
What... there are two of those pipsqueaks?!

17:08.415 --> 17:10.855
What does it mean?!

17:10.855 --> 17:12.415
Kyrie! Kyrie!

17:12.415 --> 17:13.255
What's happening?

17:13.255 --> 17:15.585
Snap out of it, bear-o!

17:16.925 --> 17:18.355
Kyrie!

17:21.025 --> 17:22.785
Toppy?

17:23.625 --> 17:25.595
Where's Morte's little brother?

17:25.595 --> 17:27.465
That was a dream, bear-o!

17:27.465 --> 17:28.705
A dream?

17:28.705 --> 17:32.275
We must be in the Labyrinth of Memories, bear-o!

17:32.275 --> 17:34.305
Labyrinth of Memories?

17:34.305 --> 17:37.715
I've heard stories about a
mysterious cave in Dragon Valley...

17:37.715 --> 17:42.145
that makes people see
visions of things from their past, bear-o.

17:42.145 --> 17:44.585
This is that cave, bear-o!

17:44.585 --> 17:46.155
Things from their past...

17:46.155 --> 17:50.425
All those mummies of beastmen and
humans we saw lying around in the cave...

17:50.425 --> 17:54.325
They got caught up in visions of the
past inside this Labyrinth of Memories!

17:54.325 --> 17:57.295
They couldn't escape, so they wound up
withering away and dying here, bear-o!

17:57.295 --> 18:00.965
But I was never in that place...

18:00.965 --> 18:03.795
and I never met Morte's brother.

18:06.835 --> 18:08.305
Where's Morte?!

18:08.305 --> 18:13.145
Morte's gotta be in here somewhere,
trapped in visions of her own past, bear-o.

18:13.145 --> 18:16.645
If we don't hurry and save her, she'll
wind up just like those mummies, bear-o!

18:16.645 --> 18:21.755
And you know what? Reve went
crazy and ate a whole bunch of nuts!

18:21.755 --> 18:24.495
He ate so many that he couldn't even move!

18:24.495 --> 18:25.795
Well, what about you, Sis?

18:25.795 --> 18:28.365
- You know you ate more than I did!
- Morte!

18:28.365 --> 18:30.625
Morte!

18:30.625 --> 18:33.835
- Hey, Sis... someone's calling for you.
- Morte! Morte!

18:33.835 --> 18:35.635
Don't you have to go, then?

18:35.635 --> 18:39.375
No, I'm gonna stay right here forever.

18:39.375 --> 18:41.505
I wanna stay right here!

18:41.505 --> 18:43.105
I'm not going anywhere!

18:43.105 --> 18:45.305
Morte!

18:50.345 --> 18:53.015
The Destruct Code...

18:53.015 --> 18:55.485
Two of those pipsqueaks...

18:55.485 --> 18:59.295
and the Labyrinth of Memories...

18:59.295 --> 19:03.165
Now I see it... so that's what it was!

19:03.165 --> 19:04.685
There she is, bear-o!

19:06.195 --> 19:08.405
Morte! Hang in there, bear-o!

19:08.405 --> 19:09.405
Morte!

19:09.405 --> 19:10.975
Snap out of it, bear-o!

19:10.975 --> 19:11.875
Morte!

19:11.875 --> 19:13.575
Stop calling my name!

19:13.575 --> 19:15.475
I wanna stay here!

19:15.475 --> 19:18.535
Morte...

19:18.875 --> 19:21.505
Morte!

19:26.885 --> 19:31.225
It looks like it's time for
us to say goodbye, Morte.

19:31.225 --> 19:35.395
No! I'm gonna stay here with
Reve and Daddy and Mommy!

19:35.395 --> 19:37.665
I wanna stay here!

19:37.665 --> 19:40.595
Morte, you've already
figured it out, haven't you?

19:40.595 --> 19:45.405
This is a memory of days
long gone. It's not the real world.

19:45.405 --> 19:49.545
I know! The real world is a stupid
place that's better off not even existing!

19:49.545 --> 19:53.615
Who wouldn't rather live here
inside a memory of the family they love?!

19:53.615 --> 19:56.185
Morte!

19:58.115 --> 19:59.855
Watch out!

19:59.855 --> 20:01.085
You alright, bear-o?

20:01.085 --> 20:01.855
I'm fine. Ow-ow-ow...

20:01.855 --> 20:04.395
This place is dangerous!
We need to get out of here, bear-o!

20:04.395 --> 20:07.895
I can hear those desperate voices.

20:07.895 --> 20:10.595
In your travels with those two...

20:10.595 --> 20:15.805
I'm sure you met plenty of people
trying desperately to just live, Morte.

20:15.805 --> 20:18.435
And this world that all those people live in...

20:18.435 --> 20:23.145
Is it really just a stupid place
that's better off not even existing?

20:23.145 --> 20:28.585
We're gonna get flattened while
Morte's still out cold! That can't happen!

20:28.585 --> 20:31.485
The world keeps right on changing...

20:31.485 --> 20:36.725
and even if some things are bad now,
you can always work on changing them.

20:36.725 --> 20:38.725
- As long as there are people like those two.
- It's crumbling faster than ever, bear-o!

20:38.725 --> 20:42.495
I don't wanna get flattened!

20:42.495 --> 20:44.325
Just look at us...

20:44.325 --> 20:47.935
Even we managed to change
the world, in our own small way.

20:47.935 --> 20:50.595
The proof is sitting right here.

20:54.305 --> 20:57.505
It's you, Morte.

20:58.275 --> 20:59.415
Me?

20:59.415 --> 21:06.355
That's right. After this, you guys are
going to change the world even more.

21:06.355 --> 21:10.185
For our sake if nothing else,
please live your real life, Morte.

21:10.185 --> 21:15.825
And go on to build the kind of future
where everyone can live in happiness.

21:17.835 --> 21:21.105
But wait! Dad! Mom!

21:21.105 --> 21:24.975
Sis, I'm sorry I couldn't keep my promise.

21:24.975 --> 21:30.375
But you're not alone anymore,
so I think you're gonna be okay.

21:30.375 --> 21:32.275
Reve! Wait!

21:32.275 --> 21:35.005
Wait, Dad! Mom!

21:37.715 --> 21:39.115
Watch out, bear-o!

21:46.655 --> 21:49.395
We made it, bear-o.

21:49.395 --> 21:51.195
We're outside!

21:53.995 --> 21:56.205
Morte! Are you awake, bear-o?

21:56.205 --> 21:57.735
I'm so glad!

21:57.735 --> 22:02.375
Kyrie... Toppy...

22:02.375 --> 22:04.745
Seems we found you...

22:04.745 --> 22:07.345
You Destruction Committee scoundrels!

22:07.345 --> 22:11.975
Now then... hand over the
Destruct Code, nice and easy!

22:21.055 --> 22:24.565
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.565 --> 22:27.695
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.695 --> 22:33.775
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.775 --> 22:36.905
afuredasu kioku

22:36.905 --> 22:40.115
Gareki no you ni

22:40.115 --> 22:46.115
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.115 --> 22:49.355
Meguriau inochi

22:49.355 --> 22:52.425
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.425 --> 22:55.565
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.565 --> 22:58.695
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.695 --> 23:10.805
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.645 --> 23:17.485
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.485 --> 23:20.485
change the world hitotsu janai

23:20.485 --> 23:26.055
Namima no mukou haruka na tabi e

23:26.055 --> 23:29.625
Dakara around the world ikiru kodou

23:29.625 --> 23:33.165
To the end of the world kaze ni hibike

23:33.165 --> 23:39.135
Sono saki ni aru

23:39.135 --> 23:50.745
yakusoku no chi, tadoritsukeru made

23:52.115 --> 23:54.585
My family is never coming back.

23:54.585 --> 23:57.155
That girl is never coming back.

23:57.155 --> 23:59.995
The past is never coming back.

23:59.995 --> 24:02.265
The mysteries of the
Destruct Code will be revealed.

24:02.265 --> 24:04.195
But as we face an ever-disintegrating world...

24:04.195 --> 24:06.935
what fate now awaits us?

24:06.935 --> 24:09.765
Next time on World
Destruction... Final Episode:

24:09.765 --> 24:11.635
"There Are Two Kinds of Futures."

24:11.635 --> 24:12.875
Will it be destruction?

24:12.875 --> 24:14.335
Will it be salvation?

24:14.335 --> 24:15.505
Will it be a bear?

24:15.505 --> 24:17.775
That's not two kinds, now is it?

24:17.775 --> 24:18.975
Bear-o?
